title: Recruitment Drive
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and recruitment_timer <= 0
on-arrival: recruitment_timer = 3; month_actions += 1
frequency: 300
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs

= Recruitment Drive

[? if year = 1919 or (year = 1920 and month < 4) : Thousands of workers are disappointed in Ebert's republic. ?][? if year = 1920 and month >= 4 : After the Kapp days, many workers want a party that will fight. ?][? if year >= 1921 : The party has become a mass party, and it must keep growing or it will shrink. ?] A recruitment drive could bring new members in, but only the districts loyal to the Zentrale will put real effort into it.

Members in loyal districts: [+ loyal_share_display +]%.

- @drive: Fund a recruitment drive.
- @tested: Admit only tested militants.
- @local: Leave recruitment to the districts.
- @easy_discard

@drive
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Loyal districts grow faster than defiant ones.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    var grow = Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] >= 50 ? 0.15 : 0.05;
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1 + grow;
}
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Organisers fan out to factories and labour exchanges. The loyal districts report a stream of new members; the others take the money and do as they please.

@tested
subtitle: Slow growth, but the new members are fighters who answer to the party.
on-arrival: {!
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.02;
}
Q.unity += 3;
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

A party of action, not of dues-payers. Each new member must be vouched for by two comrades who have seen them in a strike or on the streets.

@local
on-arrival: {!
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.04;
    Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] -= 2;
}
!}

The districts recruit in their own way and in their own image.
